WebGPU: a 3D texture's image view stays 3D

A compute image binding that names a layer range got a 2D array view. A 3D texture has no layers, and WebGPU
refuses a 2D array view of one, so the bind group was invalid, and so was every command buffer that used it.
OpenGL takes a layer range to bind every slice of a 3D level; this backend now keeps the 3D view of a 3D
texture whatever range the binding names.

diff --git a/src/renderer_webgpu.cpp b/src/renderer_webgpu.cpp
--- a/src/renderer_webgpu.cpp
+++ b/src/renderer_webgpu.cpp
@@ -4240,9 +4240,12 @@ WGPU_IMPORT
 								&& 0 != (resolvedFlags & BGFX_SAMPLER_SAMPLE_STENCIL)
 								;
 
+							// A 3D texture has no layers: its image view stays 3D whatever layer range the binding
+							// names (OpenGL takes one to bind every slice of a level).
 							const WGPUTextureViewDimension viewDimension = _isCompute
 								&& Binding::Image == bind.m_type
 								&& UINT16_MAX != bind.m_numLayers
+								&& WGPUTextureViewDimension_3D != texture.m_viewDimension
 								? WGPUTextureViewDimension_2DArray
 								: shaderBind.viewDimension
 								;
